{
 "acknowledged_limitations": [
  "SAMPLE SIZE: n=10 questions per sample, 20 total, each an independent 3-arm run \u2014 NOT the full 71-question multi-session tail of the s[150:250] slice.",
  "chunk_evidence_recall@k is null under --retrieval-only --mock, so the raw-chunk reader surface is UNMEASURED (unchanged from the previous receipt).",
  "--retrieval-only --mock exits rc=1 in _print_summary (pre-existing bug, filed separately); the report JSON is written before that.",
  "CROSS-CAMPAIGN ABSOLUTES ARE NOT COMPARABLE. Compared with the superseded receipt (same cohorts, same substrate), the OFF arm reproduces EXACTLY per question (all 20: pool_size, session_recall@5, evidence_recall@5, reader_surface@5, top-107 ids and order identical), while the injected arms reproduce on 19/20 questions and differ on S2 3c1045c8 (session_recall@5 0.5 -> 1.0). Read the arm deltas as WITHIN-RUN; do not difference absolutes across campaigns.",
  "REPRODUCIBILITY PROBE ON THE ONE DIVERGENT QUESTION (S2 3c1045c8). The divergence is a SEED-ORDER difference, not a code effect: the two campaigns' seeded_sessions lists hold the SAME 5 sessions in a different order (positions 2/3 swapped), and the seed order is first-seen pool rank, so the base pool's ORDER at the C4 insertion point differed even though the reported ranked_ids (a stable final sort) are byte-identical. Three independent FRESH single-question runs at this revision are stable at the new value (1.0), and a re-run with the WITH DISTINCT s barrier REMOVED is byte-identical to the barrier-on run \u2014 the only source change between the two revisions is result-neutral. The residual is harness-side: the eval's pre-sort pool order is not pinned.",
  "FULL-SAMPLE REPEATABILITY AT THIS REVISION (evidence, not a caveat). The whole S2 injection-only arm was re-run TWICE independently (fresh graphs, same cohort, same flags, seedless checkpoints): session_recall@5 (and therefore recall_all@5) is identical on 10/10 questions in BOTH repeats, and the second repeat is byte-identical in the top-5 ORDER on all 10 (the first permutes the order of two already-present items on 2 questions without changing any metric). So the \u00a73c1045c8 divergence is confined to the cross-campaign seed order, not to this revision.",
  "ARM ISOLATION IS A PER-QUESTION WIPE, NOT ONE DB PER ARM. The docker:// URI's path is the BASE graph name, which the eval's per-question namespace (team_default__default__<qid>) overrides \u2014 so the three arms share graph NAMES on the :6399 server and the runner script's GRAPH.DELETE <dbbase> is a no-op. Effective isolation comes from run.py's gated per-question wipe (MATCH (n) WHERE n.lme_question_id = $q DETACH DELETE n) followed by a full re-ingest; ingest_latency_ms of 27-84 s per question per arm confirms the re-ingest actually happened (no cache hit). A refused wipe (live/stale run marker) would leak the previous arm's state; no marker file was present in the arm work dirs, so the wipe ran. Recorded because the superseded receipt claims 'ONE DB PER ARM', which is not what the mechanism does.",
  "PROCESS-LEVEL LATENCY IS NOT A COST PROXY IN THIS CAMPAIGN. The machine was under fleet load: OFF-arm retrieval latency is 110.2 ms (S1) / 90.8 ms (S2) here versus 69.4 / 57.7 ms in the superseded receipt on IDENTICAL code. Use the ISOLATED C4 block cost (session_reinjection_stats.latency_ms = fetch + annotate + merge only) for the arm's cost: 6.4-9.0 ms mean, p95 <= 13.5 ms.",
  "The dedicated :6399 instance was used because the shared :6379 instance was at its 512 MB maxmemory cap (writes failed) and :6380 was concurrently in use by another test lane (its logs show an active defrag on foreign graphs). :6380 and :6379 runs aborted with ingest OutOfMemoryError / health-check failures; their reports are NOT used.",
  "Turn points have no per-turn index property, so the fetch's deterministic order for turns is coalesce(lme_chunk_index,-1) = -1 for every turn, then p.id LEXICOGRAPHIC (t0, t1, t10, t11, ... t2). The injected turn SET is therefore deterministic but not chronological. Unchanged from the shipped order clause; recorded.",
  "The injected turn points are NOT clawed back by the C5 chunk re-cap (dedup_pool counts only is_raw_chunk hits), so the total budget is the only injection-volume guard at the default grain."
 ],
