   "verdict": "MECHANISM SURVIVES; BYTE-IDENTITY DOES NOT. At turn grain the guard-ablated top-5 is not byte-identical to OFF (S1 7/10 questions identical, S2 10/10). EVERY id that enters the top-5 is a BASE item already present in OFF's ranked pool (2/2 membership changes; the remaining diffs are pure reorders) - ZERO injected items enter hits[:5] without the guard. So the injected items are the TRIGGER (they fire the guard), not the entering items. The ablated arm's own metric contribution is sample-dependent: inj_only is +0.10 recall_all@5 on S1 and 0.00 on S2, +0.05 pooled, so a single-sample reading would credit the guard with a swing that is not there. This is also the falsifier most exposed to the harness residual recorded under acknowledged_limitations: one S2 question (3c1045c8) does not reproduce across campaigns because its seed ORDER differs, and that question is one of the 3 whose top-5 differs between OFF and inj_only."
